-- l4 batch over rules that take a TYPICALLY default at a NAMED site
-- (TYPICALLY-ONE-BEHAVIOUR-SPEC.md W4 for a rule's input, W5 for a record's
-- field). The exported rule has an input of its own called `rate`, the same
-- spelling as the input `scaled` leaves out: the answer must list the default
-- `scaled` took, under `scaled`, and never the request's `rate`.

DECLARE Config
  HAS timeout IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 30
      retries IS A NUMBER

GIVEN rate IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 3
      base IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
scaled MEANS rate TIMES base

@export default Combine the pieces
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      rate IS A NUMBER
      use IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE combine IS
  IF use
  THEN (scaled WITH base IS n) PLUS (Config WITH retries IS rate)'s timeout
  ELSE 0
